IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa20-part26`
IMPORT `coa20-part27-merger`
IMPORT `coa-proc-merger`

-- coa-proc-merger-court-wait.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 27, Chapter 2, ss 915 to 918: the steps and the clocks of the routes that excuse a meeting of members of a merging
-- company, written as regulative rules over the Boolean encoding in coa20-part27-merger.l4. Lines 12691-12784 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
-- The unit is s 917 (the court's order that no meeting of any of the merging companies is required, where all the relevant securities of the transferor company are held by the transferee company)
-- and, because the same one-month wait appears in them, ss 916 and 918 (the transferee company's meeting is not required). Sections 915, 915A and 917A give no time and no step of their own: they are
-- gates, already called in coa-proc-merger.l4, and nothing is added for them.
-- The gates are the existing functions: s 917(1), s 917(2), s 917(3) of coa20-part27-merger.l4, the calendar-month helpers `s 906(3) the date one month after` and `s 906(3) the date one month before`
-- of coa20-part26.l4, and the scheme record and the merger gates of coa-proc-merger.l4. Nothing here edits those modules, and the rules of coa-proc-merger.l4 are not called.
--
-- What the one-month wait is counted from. Section 917(3A) counts it BACKWARDS from the date of the court's order: the notice of receipt must have been published "at least one month before the date of the
-- court's order". Read forwards, the court's order cannot be dated before the first date that is one calendar month after the publication of the notice. So day 0 of the rule for s 917 is the day the registrar
-- published the notice of receipt, and the days that the court must let pass are computed from that date. Sections 916(3A) and 918(2A) count the same month back from the date of the first meeting of
-- the transferor company instead of from the court's order.
-- SEAMS taken as INPUTS: the date of the publication of the notice; whether the merging companies rely on the website route of s 906A and the answer of s 917(3B)(a) and (c); the answers of the second, third and
-- fourth conditions (s 917(4), (4C), (5)), which speak of the period that ends on the date of the court's order, and whether the court is satisfied.

DECLARE `ss 915-918 party` IS ONE OF
    `ss 915-918 the court`
    `ss 915-918 the transferor company`

DECLARE `ss 915-918 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 917(2) the court makes the order that no meeting of the members of any of the merging companies is required`
    `ss 916(3A) and 918(2A) the transferor company holds the first meeting of its members summoned to agree to the scheme`

-- The answers of the conditions that are read at the date of the court's order, in one record so that a trace states them once.
DECLARE `s 917 the later conditions` HAS
    `later: s 917(4) the second condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `later: s 917(4C) the third condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `later: s 917(5) the fourth condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `later: the court is satisfied that the following conditions have been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN

-- ---- the gates and the day count ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:12739 | (1) This section applies in the case of a merger by absorption where all of the relevant securities of the transferor company (or, if there is more than one transferor company, of each of them) are held by or on behalf of the transferee company.
@ref s 917(1) This section applies to a merger by absorption where all the relevant securities of the transferor company are held by the transferee company (src:12739)
GIVEN scheme IS A `ss 902-918 the scheme`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ss 915-918 section 917 applies to the scheme` MEANS
        `ss 902-918 Part 27 applies to a merger` scheme
    AND ((`s 917(1) this section applies` (`ss 902-918 the scheme is a merger by absorption` scheme) (scheme's `scheme: all of the relevant securities of each transferor company are held by or on behalf of the transferee company`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE)

-- src:12765 | (1) In the case of any merger by absorption, it is not necessary for the scheme to be approved by the members of the transferee company if the court is satisfied that the following conditions have been complied with.
@ref s 918(1) In the case of any merger by absorption (src:12765)
GIVEN scheme IS A `ss 902-918 the scheme`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ss 915-918 section 918 applies to the scheme` MEANS
        `ss 902-918 Part 27 applies to a merger` scheme
    AND (`ss 902-918 the scheme is a merger by absorption` scheme)

-- src:12717 | (2) It is not necessary for the scheme to be approved at a meeting of the members, or any class of members, of the transferee company if the court is satisfied that the following conditions have been complied with.
-- src:12765 | (1) In the case of any merger by absorption, it is not necessary for the scheme to be approved by the members of the transferee company if the court is satisfied that the following conditions have been complied with.
@ref s 916(2) and s 918(1) The transferee company need not hold a meeting if the court is satisfied that the conditions have been complied with (src:12717 and src:12765)
-- The month of ss 916(3A) and 918(2A) is a condition of that exemption only: where the transferee company does not rely on s 916(2) or s 918(1), it holds its own meeting and the transferor company's first meeting may be held on any day. The two answers are read from the scheme record.
GIVEN scheme IS A `ss 902-918 the scheme`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ss 915-918 the transferee company relies on section 916(2) or section 918(1)` MEANS
        (scheme's `scheme: s 916(2) the meeting of members of the transferee company is not required`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
     OR (scheme's `scheme: s 918(1) the meeting of members of the transferee company is not required`) EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- The first date on which the court may make its order (or the first meeting of the transferor company may be held): the first date such that the date one calendar month before it is not earlier than the
-- publication date. It is the date one calendar month after the publication, except where the later month is shorter and the library clamps the day (31 January + 1 month = 28 February, whose date one month
-- before is 28 January, which is earlier than 31 January): then it is the next day. This is the test of the existing `s 917(3A) subsection (3A) is satisfied`, run forwards.
-- src:12742 | (3A) This subsection is satisfied if publication of notice of receipt of the draft terms by the registrar took place in respect of all the merging companies at least one month before the date of the court's order.
@ref s 917(3A) Publication of notice of receipt at least one month before the date of the court's order; ss 916(3A) and 918(2A) count the same month back from the first meeting of the transferor company (src:12742)
GIVEN `the date notice of receipt of the draft terms was published` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`ss 916(3A), 917(3A) and 918(2A) the day number of the earliest date` MEANS
    IF `s 906(3) the date one month before` (`s 906(3) the date one month after` `the date notice of receipt of the draft terms was published`) AT LEAST `the date notice of receipt of the draft terms was published`
    THEN Day (`s 906(3) the date one month after` `the date notice of receipt of the draft terms was published`)
    ELSE (Day (`s 906(3) the date one month after` `the date notice of receipt of the draft terms was published`)) PLUS 1

GIVEN `the date notice of receipt of the draft terms was published` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`ss 916(3A), 917(3A) and 918(2A) the days from the publication to the earliest date` MEANS
    (`ss 916(3A), 917(3A) and 918(2A) the day number of the earliest date` `the date notice of receipt of the draft terms was published`) MINUS (Day `the date notice of receipt of the draft terms was published`)

-- ---- s 917: the court's order that no meeting is required ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:12740 | (2) It is not necessary for the scheme to be approved at a meeting of the members, or any class of members, of any of the merging companies if the court is satisfied that the following conditions have been complied with.
-- src:12741 | (3) The first condition is that either subsection (3A) or subsection (3B) is satisfied.
-- src:12742 | (3A) This subsection is satisfied if publication of notice of receipt of the draft terms by the registrar took place in respect of all the merging companies at least one month before the date of the court's order.
-- src:12743 | (3B) This subsection is satisfied if—
-- src:12744 | (a) the conditions in section 906A(2) to (4) are met in respect of each of the merging companies,
-- src:12745 | (b) in each case, the registrar published the notice mentioned in subsection (4) of that section in the Gazette at least one month before the date of the court's order, and
-- src:12746 | (c) the draft terms remained available on the website throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, that date.
-- src:12747 | (4) The second condition is that subsection (4A) or (4B) is satisfied for each of the documents listed in the applicable paragraphs of section 911(3)(a) to (f) relating to the transferee company and the transferor company (or, if there is more than one transferor company, each of them).
-- src:12753 | (4C) The third condition is that the members of the transferee company were able to obtain copies of the documents mentioned in subsection (4), or any part of those documents, on request and free of charge, throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date mentioned in subsection (3A).
-- src:12757 | (5) The fourth condition is that—
-- src:12758 | (a) one or more members of the transferee company, who together held not less than 5% of the paid-up capital of the company which carried the right to vote at general meetings of the company (excluding any shares in the company held as treasury shares) would have been able, during that period, to require a meeting of each class of members to be called for the purpose of deciding whether or not to agree to the scheme, and
-- src:12759 | (b) no such requirement was made.
@ref s 917(2), (3), (4), (4C) and (5) The court's order that no meeting of the members of any of the merging companies is required (src:12740-12759)
-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day the registrar published the notice of receipt of the draft terms in respect of the last of the merging companies; counting="at least one month before the date of the court's order": counted backwards from the order, so the order may be dated on the first date that is one calendar month after day 0 or later (the date one month before it is not earlier than day 0, the test of the existing `s 917(3A)`); the number of days to that date is computed from the publication date; the court's order itself carries no time limit, so after the wait the step is silent
-- The registrar's publication has no clock in this section: s 906(3) times it from a meeting, and with the exemption there may be no meeting summoned; s 917(3A) only asks that it took place early enough, so it is the day 0 of this rule and not a step in it.
-- FORK: s 917(3A) "in respect of all the merging companies" | day 0 is the publication date for the LAST of the merging companies, the latest of the dates, because each company's notice must be at least one month before the order | each company's date counted separately
-- FORK: s 917(3A) "at least one month before the date of the court's order" | the earliest date is the first date whose date one calendar month before is not earlier than the publication date (the existing function's test), so a notice published on 31 January allows an order from 1 March and not on 28 February | the month ends on the last day of a shorter month (28 February), or a month is thirty days
-- FORK: s 917(3A) an order dated before the wait | shown as the court's breach (BREACH BY the court) so that a trace shows the route lost; the Act does not call it a breach: the first condition is not complied with, the court cannot be satisfied, and the meetings required by s 907(1) are still required | no one's breach, the exemption is merely unavailable
-- FORK: s 917(3B)(b) the website route | the same wait and the same day 0, taken from the publication in the Gazette of the notice mentioned in s 906A(4); the rest of (3B), the conditions of s 906A(2) to (4) and the website's availability, is an input read after the wait | a separate rule for the website route
-- FORK: s 917(4), (4C), (5) | the answers are inputs read at the date of the order, because they speak of "the period beginning one month before, and ending on" the order; an answer of NOTHING is treated as not met, so the court's power is not open until the answer is known | an unknown answer leaves the power open
-- FORK: s 917(2) "if the court is satisfied" | a MAY of the court with no time limit: the text gives none, and the court need not make the order | a duty of the court to make the order once the conditions are met
GIVEN scheme IS A `ss 902-918 the scheme`
      `the date notice of receipt of the draft terms was published` IS A DATE
      `the merging companies rely on the website route of section 906A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 917(3B)(a) and (c) for the website route` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      later IS A `s 917 the later conditions`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `ss 915-918 party` `ss 915-918 act`
`s 917(2) the court's order that no meeting is required, not before the one-month wait` MEANS
    IF `ss 915-918 section 917 applies to the scheme` scheme
    THEN PARTY `ss 915-918 the court`
         SHANT `s 917(2) the court makes the order that no meeting of the members of any of the merging companies is required`
         WITHIN ((`ss 916(3A), 917(3A) and 918(2A) the days from the publication to the earliest date` `the date notice of receipt of the draft terms was published`) MINUS 1)
         HENCE (IF (`s 917(2) the meeting of members of any of the merging companies is not required`
                        (JUST TRUE)
                        (`s 917(3) the first condition is met` (IF `the merging companies rely on the website route of section 906A` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE) (IF `the merging companies rely on the website route of section 906A` THEN `the answer of s 917(3B)(a) and (c) for the website route` ELSE JUST FALSE))
                        (later's `later: s 917(4) the second condition is met`)
                        (later's `later: s 917(4C) the third condition is met`)
                        (later's `later: s 917(5) the fourth condition is met`)
                        (later's `later: the court is satisfied that the following conditions have been complied with`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
                THEN PARTY `ss 915-918 the court`
                     MAY `s 917(2) the court makes the order that no meeting of the members of any of the merging companies is required`
                     HENCE FULFILLED
                ELSE FULFILLED)
         -- Kept as a breach by the court (src:12740): the court may make the order only if "satisfied that the following conditions have been complied with", so an order made too early is a limit on the court's power and not a lapsed power of a party.
         LEST BREACH BY `ss 915-918 the court` BECAUSE "the court's order was dated less than one month after the notice of receipt of the draft terms was published (s 917(3A), or s 917(3B)(b) on the website route), so the first condition is not complied with, the court cannot be satisfied and the meetings of the members are still required (s 907(1))"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- ---- ss 916 and 918: the first meeting of the transferor company, and the transferee company's meeting ----------------------------------------

-- src:12716 | (1) This section applies in the case of a merger by absorption where 90% or more (but not all) of the relevant securities of the transferor company (or, if there is more than one transferor company, of each of them) are held by or on behalf of the transferee company.
-- src:12717 | (2) It is not necessary for the scheme to be approved at a meeting of the members, or any class of members, of the transferee company if the court is satisfied that the following conditions have been complied with.
-- src:12718 | (3) The first condition is that either subsection (3A) or subsection (3B) is satisfied.
-- src:12719 | (3A) This subsection is satisfied if publication of notice of receipt of the draft terms by the registrar took place in respect of the transferee company at least one month before the date of the first meeting of members, or any class of members, of the transferor company summoned for the purpose of agreeing to the scheme.
@ref s 916(1) to (3A) The transferee company's meeting is not required if the notice was published at least one month before the first meeting of the transferor company (src:12716-12719)
-- src:12765 | (1) In the case of any merger by absorption, it is not necessary for the scheme to be approved by the members of the transferee company if the court is satisfied that the following conditions have been complied with.
-- src:12766 | (2) The first condition is that either subsection (2A) or subsection (2B) is satisfied.
-- src:12767 | (2A) This subsection is satisfied if publication of notice of receipt of the draft terms by the registrar took place in respect of the transferee company at least one month before the date of the first meeting of members, or any class of members, of the transferor company (or, if there is more than one transferor company, any of them) summoned for the purposes of agreeing to the scheme.
@ref s 918(1) to (2A) The same, in the case of any merger by absorption (src:12765-12767)
-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day the registrar published the notice of receipt of the draft terms in respect of the transferee company; counting="at least one month before the date of the first meeting of members, or any class of members, of the transferor company": counted backwards from the meeting, so the first meeting may be held on the first date that is one calendar month after day 0 or later (the same date arithmetic as s 917(3A) above); the number of days to that date is computed from the publication date; after the wait the step is silent
-- FORK: ss 916(3A) and 918(2A) | one rule serves both sections, gated by s 918(1) (any merger by absorption), because s 916(1) (90% or more, not all) is a narrower case with the same clock and s 917 (all held) has its own anchor | a rule for each section
-- FORK: ss 916(3A) and 918(2A) the gate | the rule runs only where the transferee company relies on s 916(2) or s 918(1) (the answer of either is JUST TRUE in the scheme record), because the month is a condition of that exemption (src:12765 "it is not necessary for the scheme to be approved by the members of the transferee company if the court is satisfied that the following conditions have been complied with", src:12767 "(2A)") and not a duty on the transferor company; where neither is relied on, the transferee company holds its own meeting and an early first meeting of the transferor company is lawful | the rule binds every merger by absorption (the encoder's first reading, changed after independent review)
-- FORK: ss 916(3A) and 918(2A) a meeting held before the wait | a closed route, FULFILLED: the first condition of the transferee company's exemption is not met, so that company's meeting is required (s 907(1)); the text names no bearer, the transferor company does no wrong, and the exemption is lost | shown as the transferor company's breach (the encoder's first reading, changed after independent review)
-- FORK: ss 916(3A) and 918(2A) "the first meeting" | the date of the first meeting is the earliest of the meetings of the transferor company (or of any of them) summoned to agree to the scheme, as the existing module reads "the first meeting" | each class meeting counted separately
-- FORK: ss 916(3B)(b) and 918(2B)(b) the website route | the same wait, taken from the Gazette notice mentioned in s 906A(4); the rest of the route is the Boolean module's | a separate rule
-- Which transferee-company conditions follow (the court's satisfaction, the documents, the 5% requisition) are the answers of the existing s 916(2) and s 918(1) functions, carried in the scheme record; they are not repeated here.
GIVEN scheme IS A `ss 902-918 the scheme`
      `the date notice of receipt of the draft terms was published` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `ss 915-918 party` `ss 915-918 act`
`ss 916(3A) and 918(2A) the first meeting of the transferor company, not before the one-month wait` MEANS
    IF     (`ss 915-918 section 918 applies to the scheme` scheme)
       AND (`ss 915-918 the transferee company relies on section 916(2) or section 918(1)` scheme)
    THEN PARTY `ss 915-918 the transferor company`
         SHANT `ss 916(3A) and 918(2A) the transferor company holds the first meeting of its members summoned to agree to the scheme`
         WITHIN ((`ss 916(3A), 917(3A) and 918(2A) the days from the publication to the earliest date` `the date notice of receipt of the draft terms was published`) MINUS 1)
         HENCE (PARTY `ss 915-918 the transferor company`
                MAY `ss 916(3A) and 918(2A) the transferor company holds the first meeting of its members summoned to agree to the scheme`
                HENCE FULFILLED)
         -- Closed route, not a breach (src:12765, src:12767): the first meeting of the transferor company was held less than one month after the notice of receipt was published in respect of the transferee company, so the first condition of the transferee company's exemption is not met and that company's meeting is required (s 907(1)); the transferor company did no wrong and the exemption is lost.
         LEST FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- ---- not encoded --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- ss 915, 915A, 917A: no time and no step of their own (gates, called in coa-proc-merger.l4).
-- s 917(4A), (4B), (4C), (4D) and (5), s 916(4) to (5) and s 918(3) to (4): the availability of the documents and of copies throughout the month before the order or the meeting, and the 5% requisition, are
-- conditions of the exemption, not duties of anyone; they enter as answers read at the date of the order (s 917) or are in the scheme record (ss 916, 918). The same availability as a DUTY of the company
-- with the first meeting as the end date is `s 911(1)` in coa-proc-merger.l4.
-- The registrar's duty to publish (s 906(2)) is in coa-proc-merger.l4; with no meeting summoned it has no time.
